 "title": "No two shortest routes tie before lcm(m, f) - lcm/m - lcm/f + 1",
 "subject": "Networks of rings joined by shared contacts, read with the canonical knot test on their space-time law",
 "conclusion": "In the contact graph of rule-60 rings on every regular tiling, with m contacts per ring and f per face, no contact is reached by two shortest routes before distance lcm(m, f) - lcm/m - lcm/f + 1, so the plain first need reads every contact closer than that on time. When m = f a tie comes exactly there; elsewhere it does on every tiling read.",
